    "sig": "61253580b8",
    "ms": 1802,
    "file": "68b38d443944.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Grazie, Kaylee!",
    "voice": "lupa",
    "sig": "1200e8d792",
    "ms": 1586,
    "file": "4858dee9b19b.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Grazie, Kaylee!",
    "voice": "spina",
    "sig": "cb98c37ff1",
    "ms": 1659,
    "file": "c3bf25dd6176.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Grazie, Kaylee.",
    "voice": "cesare",
    "sig": "959ae58ccf",
    "ms": 1292,
    "file": "e198c2aa19f8.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Grazie, Kaylee!",
    "voice": "civetta",
    "sig": "61253580b8",
    "ms": 1477,
    "file": "761890793a9d.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Ciao! Can I ride?",
    "voice": "lupa",
    "sig": "1200e8d792",
    "ms": 2136,
    "file": "5253d2333bec.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Ciao! Me too!",
    "voice": "spina",
    "sig": "cb98c37ff1",
    "ms": 1605,
    "file": "56f49a6b9566.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "A ride, please.",
    "voice": "cesare",
    "sig": "959ae58ccf",
    "ms": 1688,
    "file": "644783cb6d85.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Hoo! A ride?",
    "voice": "civetta",
    "sig": "61253580b8",
    "ms": 2248,
    "file": "e52321ab548d.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "A lantern for the canal!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2057,
    "file": "41dd7441bb44.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "High water! Acqua alta!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2790,
    "file": "59eaf3fd02d9.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Low bridge! Tap Gino to duck!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2454,
    "file": "fe02bd68ccc4.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Bonk! My hat!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 2111,
    "file": "06e619499ad0.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "My hat! Grazie!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 2383,
    "file": "5b76f3d534d8.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Now take me to the mask shop!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 2404,
    "file": "51fbc4a78f9d.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "The mask shop! Let's make a mask for Carnevale!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 3677,
    "file": "e2d11dbc5ff0.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Paint one side. Watch the other side!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4034,
    "file": "f8bd6c36b294.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Now add sparkly gems!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2251,
    "file": "d4e30ba2b340.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "What a beautiful mask!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 1976,
    "file": "333851a0fc34.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Ooh! So pretty!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2645,
    "file": "8b0b398efcd2.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Tap the check when you love it!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2411,
    "file": "ee6b6a5c6f55.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Look! The canal is all lit up!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3055,
    "file": "d22487a492ac.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Fireworks for Carnevale!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 2948,
    "file": "c5c6e6936bf4.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "My accordion, for Lupa's band!",
    "voice": "gino",
    "sig": "94eab962c4",
    "ms": 3094,
    "file": "22ac7cd7c441.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Even ambulances are boats in Venice!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3329,
    "file": "cca5cdaf8167.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Brown bear sticker! Bears live in the mountains of Italy!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3501,
    "file": "7b58c2d4dc63.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Porcupine sticker! Crested porcupines live in Italy!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 5079,
    "file": "d04627838689.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Cat sticker! Lots of cats live in the old ruins of Rome!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4300,
    "file": "0530bfdfd976.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Wolf sticker! The story says a kind mama wolf took care of the twins who built Rome!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 5683,
    "file": "a9226cd7ce5a.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Pigeon sticker! Lots of pigeons live in Venice!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4778,
    "file": "cf6248a5c528.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Let's see how olive oil is made!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2775,
    "file": "e056fa5ac5de.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Let's toss a coin in the real Trevi Fountain!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3790,
    "file": "0bdfd0c6a0c3.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Look! A real Roman water bridge!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3261,
    "file": "8412395e1f18.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Let's see the real Colosseum in Rome!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3126,
    "file": "e0595ea8f84d.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Venice is a city on the water! It has more than four hundred bridges, and the buses and ambulances are boats!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 8611,
    "file": "567e42db8934.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "In Italy, people say ciao! It means hello and goodbye!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4716,
    "file": "34e29421466d.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Grazie means thank you!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4080,
    "file": "4da23d4eb99a.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "One, two, three in Italian: uno, due, tre!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2643,
    "file": "4f8a1200cf84.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Italy is shaped like a boot, kicking a ball!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4010,
    "file": "01b9290e7c68.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Italy has hot, sunny summers, and snowy mountains up north!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 5347,
    "file": "d027310d28b4.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Pizza comes from Naples, in Italy!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 2853,
    "file": "b3ca0be2c57e.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Pizza Margherita is red, white and green, like Italy's flag!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 5306,
    "file": "b49f0126ddc1.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Long ago, the Romans built roads, arenas and water bridges!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4971,
    "file": "a2f74bce0caa.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Italy has volcanoes! One is right next to Naples!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4128,
    "file": "7b9a4d420944.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Italy's flag has three stripes: green, white and red!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4294,
    "file": "0e624184787c.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Some olive trees in Italy are more than a thousand years old!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 4847,
    "file": "b9722345cb36.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "Romans wrote five like this: V!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3327,
    "file": "bc6f22a6ac84.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "The story says a kind mama wolf took care of the twins who built Rome!",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 6518,
    "file": "41939ecc40cb.mp3"
  },
  {
    "text": "This is Italy! Tap a picture to learn more.",
    "voice": "sparkle",
    "sig": "ed7dbdac3d",
    "ms": 3763,
    "file": "8c613cab3ce9.mp3"
  }
]
